## 5. Data and Persistence Contract

All new fields on existing dataclasses require safe defaults. Unknown saved fields are ignored; missing fields receive defaults. Old `NPC.from_dict` and related loaders must never raise `KeyError` because a new field is absent.

### 5.1 Required Safe Extensions

Add only after the audit confirms no equivalent exists:

| Owner | Extension | Purpose |
|---|---|---|
| `NPC` | `emotion_state` | active emotion instances: intensity, source, duration, decay, trigger/modifiers as needed |
| `NPC` | `stress` | 0–100 state, distinct from fatigue and morale |
| `NPC` | `relationship_map` | target ID → nine canonical relationship axes |
| `NPC` | `archetype_template` | debug/initialization reference only |
| `NPC` | `eval_tier`, `last_eval_tick` | current evaluation routing state |
| `NPC` | cache key/result and granular version counters | cache safety, never state authority |
| `NPC` | structured trauma runtime state, if needed | activation and recovery keyed to existing trauma tags |
| `MemoryEntry` | participants, location ID, tags, relationship deltas, confidence, source, decay rate | psychological retrieval, reliability, and decay |

New persistent objects need `schema_version`, safe serialize/deserialize behavior, and diagnostic `traits` where they are persistent domain models. Ephemeral objects such as a candidate action or situation context do not need persistent traits.

### 5.2 State Lifetime

| Lifetime | Examples |
|---|---|
| Stable | identity, personality, temperament, values, preferences |
| Semi-stable | motivations, goals, relationships, trauma profile |
| Volatile | needs, active emotions, stress, trauma activation |
| Ephemeral | situation, perceived event, appraisal, temporary scores, decision context |
| Derived/cache | behavioral patterns, legacy projections, cache entries |

Stable does not mean immutable; it means a single event cannot radically rewrite the state.

### 5.3 Required New Standalone Types Only When No Existing Analog Exists

- `PersonalityTemplate`: immutable archetype distribution; deep-copy before NPC initialization.
- `WorldEvent`: normalized event payload only if the existing event system lacks an equivalent adapter. It has deterministic ID, priority, severity, scope, sensory channel/range, source location, affected IDs, trigger type, effects, relevance, tick, and traits.
- `ActionCandidate`: ephemeral action ID, intent, target, utility/risk, emotion/value/goal fit, relationship effect, personality bias, expected consequence.
- `DecisionResult`: NPC ID, tick, selected and runner-up candidates, trace, tier, cache-hit flag, traits.

Do not create standalone models merely to duplicate `NPC`, `NPCNeeds`, `MemoryEntry`, relationships, values, or the existing Cognitive Engine.

