## 6. Personality Templates

Provide at least these eight distribution-based templates. Store a template reference for debugging only; template instances must never share mutable state with NPCs.

| ID | Bias | Value tendency | Risk | Dominant motivation |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| `cautious_scholar` | analytical, high rationality, low aggression | knowledge > safety > autonomy/honor | low | curiosity/safety |
| `reckless_adventurer` | low patience, high courage, novelty seeking | freedom > adventure/glory > achievement/wealth | high | achievement/autonomy |
| `devoted_knight` | high loyalty and altruism, disciplined | duty/honor > loyalty/family > protection | controlled | loyalty/meaning |
| `cynical_mercenary` | high cunning, low altruism, guarded | survival/wealth > autonomy/power | calculated | survival/wealth |
| `ambitious_noble` | high pride and cunning | status > power > achievement/wealth | calculated-high | status/power |
| `gentle_healer` | high altruism and patience | compassion/life > family/belonging/community | low | belonging/affection |
| `paranoid_survivor` | high suspicion and neuroticism | survival > safety > autonomy/self | very low | survival/safety |
| `zealous_inquisitor` | high aggression/rationality, conviction-driven | faith > order > justice | context-dependent | meaning |

Each template specifies personality distributions, value default order, motivation, risk range, temperament baseline, trauma-susceptibility tags, and traits. Use deterministic seeded sampling for initialization; clamp values to valid ranges. Do not use random selection during decision-making. Same-template NPCs must diverge through variation, background, memories, trauma, relationships, preferences, values, knowledge, and goals.

