## 10. Tier Router, Event Routing, and Cache

### 10.1 Tiers

| Tier | Conditions | Allowed work | Budget |
|---|---|---|---|
| 1 | no direct interaction, perceivable event, critical deadline, or trauma context | schedule, routine, location/time, passive emotion decay/stress recovery | O(1) |
| 2 | perceivable local event: noise, fire, combat, theft, death, anomaly | detection, minimal threat/interest appraisal, minimal emotion/stress update | under 5 ms; no RAG/LLM/full pipeline |
| 3 | direct dialogue/negotiation/threat/betrayal/trauma/goal-critical/major-resource/combat decision | full 12 stages, RAG, optional LLM, trace | under 200 ms excluding async external work |

Use the existing event hook. Route as affected-NPC filter → distance/sensory gate → tier classification → tier handler. Perceived intensity accounts for severity, distance attenuation, sensory range, channel, and NPC sensitivity. Coalesce same trigger type and source location within three ticks, then fan out the result. Never perform synchronous RAG or LLM work in the game tick loop.

### 10.2 Decision Cache

Cache only decision results, never truth. Use NPC-local keys based on NPC ID, situation/event hash, relevant world state version, memory version, relationship version, and optionally goal/emotion/trauma versions.

Invalidate on emotion delta at least 10, relationship delta at least 5, new memory, world version change, goal change, trauma activation, material need change, critical event, or capability/resource change. Cache hits never bypass current version validation or authoritative state updates.

