## 11. LLM Boundary and Context Projection

Python supplies an expression-oriented, validated projection: selected action, dialogue intent, emotional expression, relevant relationship context, a few summarized relevant memories, known situation facts, allowed knowledge scope, speech style, value/coping constraints.

Do not dump full internal state, hidden world facts, raw complete personality/truama memory values, arbitrary future events, or direct mutation instructions into the LLM prompt.

LLM output may contain dialogue, narration, tone, subtext, emotional expression, action candidates, social-interpretation proposals, or query-expansion proposals. Every state-bearing implication follows:

```text
LLM proposal → Python parse → schema/world/capability/knowledge validation
→ event or delta → authoritative commit
```

LLM hallucinations cannot change world facts, NPC memories, beliefs, relationships, goals, or decisions. If the LLM fails, decision processing continues and uses deterministic/template text output.

